<title>USA: Litton unit wins $50 mln contract.</title>
<headline>Litton unit wins $50 mln contract.</headline>
<dateline>WOODLAND HILLS, Calif. 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Litton Industries Inc unit PRC Wednesday said it has been named one of four winners of a Defense Logistics agency contract that could be worth over $50 million for the company.</p>
<p>Under the contract, PRC will help migrate computer information systems from a mainframe to a client/server network. The contract is known as the DLA System Design Center Software Engineering &amp; Technical Support contract, Litton said in a statement.</p>
<p>This contract covers a five year period.</p>
